    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d581">

                <pb facs="0602" n="494" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg494"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102H/479: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-28T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 28—9:45
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>92. With reference to the Legation’s despatch No. 773 of 1926 concerning Harbin
                    Municipality, I ask authority to approve a recommendation now made to me by
                    Hanson that “American firms and citizens be requested to pay through the
                    consulate to the municipality or Commissioner for Foreign Affairs voluntarily
                    contributions at the same rates as those of taxes levied on nationals whose
                    Governments adhered to the 1914 municipal agreement<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d581-f1"/> and collected at the time the old municipality created by
                    this agreement was in power.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d581-f1" n="62" xml:id="d581-f1-content">
                <p>For text of agreement between the British and Russian Governments respecting
                    municipal administration and taxation within the area of the Chinese Eastern
                    Railway, signed at Harbin, Apr. 17/30, 1914, see <hi rendition="#italic">British
                        and Foreign State Papers</hi>, 1914 (pt. <hi rendition="#italic">ii</hi>),
                    vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">cviii</hi>, p. 380.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
